    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>cf-boundary</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>ContinuantFiatBoundary</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b is a continuant fiat boundary = Def. b is an immaterial entity that is of zero, one or two dimensions and does not include a spatial region as part. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [029-001])</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">BFO 2 Reference: In BFO 1.1 the assumption was made that the external surface of a material entity such as a cell could be treated as if it were a boundary in the mathematical sense. The new document propounds the view that when we talk about external surfaces of material objects in this way then we are talking about something fiat. To be dealt with in a future version: fiat boundaries at different levels of granularity.More generally, the focus in discussion of boundaries in BFO 2.0 is now on fiat boundaries, which means: boundaries for which there is no assumption that they coincide with physical discontinuities. The ontology of boundaries becomes more closely allied with the ontology of regions.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">BFO 2 Reference: a continuant fiat boundary is a boundary of some material entity (for example: the plane separating the Northern and Southern hemispheres; the North Pole), or it is a boundary of some immaterial entity (for example of some portion of airspace). Three basic kinds of continuant fiat boundary can be distinguished (together with various combination kinds [29</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Continuant fiat boundary doesn&apos;t have a closure axiom because the subclasses don&apos;t necessarily exhaust all possibilites. An example would be the mereological sum of two-dimensional continuant fiat boundary and a one dimensional continuant fiat boundary that doesn&apos;t overlap it. The situation is analogous to temporal and spatial regions.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000601 xml:lang="en">Every continuant fiat boundary is located at some spatial region at every time at which it exists</obo:IAO_0000601>
        <obo:IAO_0000602>(iff (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ImmaterialEntity a) (exists (b) (and (or (ZeroDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (OneDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (TwoDimensionalSpatialRegion b)) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))) (not (exists (c t) (and (SpatialRegion c) (continuantPartOfAt c a t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [029-001] </obo:IAO_0000602>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">continuant fiat boundary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">b is a continuant fiat boundary = Def. b is an immaterial entity that is of zero, one or two dimensions and does not include a spatial region as part. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [029-001])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/029-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">Continuant fiat boundary doesn&apos;t have a closure axiom because the subclasses don&apos;t necessarily exhaust all possibilites. An example would be the mereological sum of two-dimensional continuant fiat boundary and a one dimensional continuant fiat boundary that doesn&apos;t overlap it. The situation is analogous to temporal and spatial regions.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/0000008"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>(iff (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ImmaterialEntity a) (exists (b) (and (or (ZeroDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (OneDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (TwoDimensionalSpatialRegion b)) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))) (not (exists (c t) (and (SpatialRegion c) (continuantPartOfAt c a t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [029-001] </owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/029-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000141">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
        <owl:disjointWith>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </owl:disjointWith>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>immaterial</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>ImmaterialEntity</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">BFO 2 Reference: Immaterial entities are divided into two subgroups:boundaries and sites, which bound, or are demarcated in relation, to material entities, and which can thus change location, shape and size and as their material hosts move or change shape or size (for example: your nasal passage; the hold of a ship; the boundary of Wales (which moves with the rotation of the Earth) [38, 7, 10</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">immaterial entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000147"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>1d-cf-boundary</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>OneDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">The Equator</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">all geopolitical boundaries</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">all lines of latitude and longitude</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">the line separating the outer surface of the mucosa of the lower lip from the outer surface of the skin of the chin.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">the median sulcus of your tongue</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000600 xml:lang="en">a one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary is a continuous fiat line whose location is defined in relation to some material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [032-001])</obo:IAO_0000600>
        <obo:IAO_0000602>(iff (OneDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (OneDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [032-001] </obo:IAO_0000602>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000600"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">a one-dimensional continuant fiat boundary is a continuous fiat line whose location is defined in relation to some material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [032-001])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/032-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>(iff (OneDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (OneDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [032-001] </owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/032-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000144 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000144">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000182"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>process-profile</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>ProcessProfile</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">On a somewhat higher level of complexity are what we shall call rate process profiles, which are the targets of selective abstraction focused not on determinate quality magnitudes plotted over time, but rather on certain ratios between these magnitudes and elapsed times. A speed process profile, for example, is represented by a graph plotting against time the ratio of distance covered per unit of time. Since rates may change, and since such changes, too, may have rates of change, we have to deal here with a hierarchy of process profile universals at successive levels</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">One important sub-family of rate process profiles is illustrated by the beat or frequency profiles of cyclical processes, illustrated by the 60 beats per minute beating process of John’s heart, or the 120 beats per minute drumming process involved in one of John’s performances in a rock band, and so on. Each such process includes what we shall call a beat process profile instance as part, a subtype of rate process profile in which the salient ratio is not distance covered but rather number of beat cycles per unit of time. Each beat process profile instance instantiates the determinable universal beat process profile. But it also instantiates multiple more specialized universals at lower levels of generality, selected from   rate process profilebeat process profileregular beat process profile3 bpm beat process profile4 bpm beat process profileirregular beat process profileincreasing beat process profileand so on.In the case of a regular beat process profile, a rate can be assigned in the simplest possible fashion by dividing the number of cycles by the length of the temporal region occupied by the beating process profile as a whole. Irregular process profiles of this sort, for example as identified in the clinic, or in the readings on an aircraft instrument panel, are often of diagnostic significance.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">The simplest type of process profiles are what we shall call ‘quality process profiles’, which are the process profiles which serve as the foci of the sort of selective abstraction that is involved when measurements are made of changes in single qualities, as illustrated, for example, by process profiles of mass, temperature, aortic pressure, and so on.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b is a process_profile =Def. there is some process c such that b process_profile_of c (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [093-002])</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000600 xml:lang="en">b process_profile_of c holds when b proper_occurrent_part_of c&amp; there is some proper_occurrent_part d of c which has no parts in common with b &amp; is mutually dependent on b&amp; is such that b, c and d occupy the same temporal region (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [094-005])</obo:IAO_0000600>
        <obo:IAO_0000602>(forall (x y) (if (processProfileOf x y) (and (properContinuantPartOf x y) (exists (z t) (and (properOccurrentPartOf z y) (TemporalRegion t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion x t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion y t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion z t) (not (exists (w) (and (occurrentPartOf w x) (occurrentPartOf w z))))))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [094-005] </obo:IAO_0000602>
        <obo:IAO_0000602>(iff (ProcessProfile a) (exists (b) (and (Process b) (processProfileOf a b)))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [093-002] </obo:IAO_0000602>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">process profile</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">b is a process_profile =Def. there is some process c such that b process_profile_of c (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [093-002])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/093-002"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000600"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">b process_profile_of c holds when b proper_occurrent_part_of c&amp; there is some proper_occurrent_part d of c which has no parts in common with b &amp; is mutually dependent on b&amp; is such that b, c and d occupy the same temporal region (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [094-005])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/094-005"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>(forall (x y) (if (processProfileOf x y) (and (properContinuantPartOf x y) (exists (z t) (and (properOccurrentPartOf z y) (TemporalRegion t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion x t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion y t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion z t) (not (exists (w) (and (occurrentPartOf w x) (occurrentPartOf w z))))))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [094-005] </owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/094-005"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>(iff (ProcessProfile a) (exists (b) (and (Process b) (processProfileOf a b)))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [093-002] </owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/093-002"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000145 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000145">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>r-quality</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>RelationalQuality</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">John’s role of husband to Mary is dependent on Mary’s role of wife to John, and both are dependent on the object aggregate comprising John and Mary as member parts joined together through the relational quality of being married.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">a marriage bond, an instance of requited love, an obligation between one person and another.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">b is a relational quality = Def. for some independent continuants c, d and for some time t: b quality_of c at t &amp; b quality_of d at t. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [057-001])</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000602>(iff (RelationalQuality a) (exists (b c t) (and (IndependentContinuant b) (IndependentContinuant c) (qualityOfAt a b t) (qualityOfAt a c t)))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [057-001] </obo:IAO_0000602>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">relational quality</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000145"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">b is a relational quality = Def. for some independent continuants c, d and for some time t: b quality_of c at t &amp; b quality_of d at t. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [057-001])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/057-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000145"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>(iff (RelationalQuality a) (exists (b c t) (and (IndependentContinuant b) (IndependentContinuant c) (qualityOfAt a b t) (qualityOfAt a c t)))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [057-001] </owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/057-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>2d-cf-boundary</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>TwoDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000600 xml:lang="en">a two-dimensional continuant fiat boundary (surface) is a self-connected fiat surface whose location is defined in relation to some material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [033-001])</obo:IAO_0000600>
        <obo:IAO_0000602>(iff (TwoDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (TwoDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [033-001] </obo:IAO_0000602>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">two-dimensional continuant fiat boundary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000600"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">a two-dimensional continuant fiat boundary (surface) is a self-connected fiat surface whose location is defined in relation to some material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [033-001])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/033-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>(iff (TwoDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (TwoDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [033-001] </owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/033-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000147 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000147">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>0d-cf-boundary</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>ZeroDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">the geographic North Pole</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">the point of origin of some spatial coordinate system.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">the quadripoint where the boundaries of Colorado, Utah, New Mexico, and Arizona meet</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">zero dimension continuant fiat boundaries are not spatial points. Considering the example &apos;the quadripoint where the boundaries of Colorado, Utah, New Mexico, and Arizona meet&apos; : There are many frames in which that point is zooming through many points in space. Whereas, no matter what the frame, the quadripoint is always in the same relation to the boundaries of Colorado, Utah, New Mexico, and Arizona.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000600 xml:lang="en">a zero-dimensional continuant fiat boundary is a fiat point whose location is defined in relation to some material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [031-001])</obo:IAO_0000600>
        <obo:IAO_0000602>(iff (ZeroDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (ZeroDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [031-001] </obo:IAO_0000602>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">zero-dimensional continuant fiat boundary</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000147"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">zero dimension continuant fiat boundaries are not spatial points. Considering the example &apos;the quadripoint where the boundaries of Colorado, Utah, New Mexico, and Arizona meet&apos; : There are many frames in which that point is zooming through many points in space. Whereas, no matter what the frame, the quadripoint is always in the same relation to the boundaries of Colorado, Utah, New Mexico, and Arizona.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/0000001"/>
        <rdfs:comment>requested by Melanie Courtot</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://groups.google.com/d/msg/bfo-owl-devel/s9Uug5QmAws/ZDRnpiIi_TUJ"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000147"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000600"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">a zero-dimensional continuant fiat boundary is a fiat point whose location is defined in relation to some material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [031-001])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/031-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000147"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>(iff (ZeroDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (ZeroDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [031-001] </owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/031-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000148 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000148">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000008"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>0d-t-region</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>ZeroDimensionalTemporalRegion</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">a temporal region that is occupied by a process boundary</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">right now</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">the moment at which a child is born</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">the moment at which a finger is detached in an industrial accident</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">the moment of death.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">temporal instant.</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000600 xml:lang="en">A zero-dimensional temporal region is a temporal region that is without extent. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [102-001])</obo:IAO_0000600>
        <obo:IAO_0000602>(forall (x) (if (ZeroDimensionalTemporalRegion x) (TemporalRegion x))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [102-001] </obo:IAO_0000602>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">zero-dimensional temporal region</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000600"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A zero-dimensional temporal region is a temporal region that is without extent. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [102-001])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/102-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>(forall (x) (if (ZeroDimensionalTemporalRegion x) (TemporalRegion x))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [102-001] </owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/102-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000182 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000182">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000179>history</obo:BFO_0000179>
        <obo:BFO_0000180>History</obo:BFO_0000180>
        <obo:IAO_0000600 xml:lang="en">A history is a process that is the sum of the totality of processes taking place in the spatiotemporal region occupied by a material entity or site, including processes on the surface of the entity or within the cavities to which it serves as host. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [138-001])</obo:IAO_0000600>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">history</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000182"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000600"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A history is a process that is the sum of the totality of processes taking place in the spatiotemporal region occupied by a material entity or site, including processes on the surface of the entity or within the cavities to which it serves as host. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [138-001])</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0010000 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/axiom/138-001"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000026 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000026">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000312"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000110"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A material entity processed by human activity with an intent to produce it.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">In the COB 2024 workshop there was much disagreement about this label.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">processed material entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000035 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000035">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000082"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000055"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000260"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">completely executed planned process</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cob.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">completely executed planned process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000082 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000082">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">planned process</obo:IAO_0000111>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A process that is initiated by an agent who intends to carry out a plan to achieve an objective through one or more actions as described in a plan specification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cob.owl"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">planned process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000110 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000110">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000035"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000293"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A completely executed planned process that intends to output material entities from input material entities</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">material processing</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000502 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000502">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">characteristic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0001300 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0001300">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000026"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002215"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A processed material entity which is designed to be capable of a process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">device</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000001 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000001">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An information content entity that represents the complete set of metabolic fluxes (reaction rates) in a biological system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>fluxomics</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>fluxome</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000002 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000002">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000125"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000159"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000227"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An information content entity that contains files to determine the rates of metabolic reactions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Could be moved to role</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:comment>It generally includes the model of metabolic networks and experimental data.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>fluxomics data</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000123"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000124"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux of a metabolic reaction that occurs within a metabolic network model boundries.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>internal flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000004">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000123"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux that is the rate of a transport process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>transport rate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>transport flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000005 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000005">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000166"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000166"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0003301"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000126"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0003301"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000278"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A chemical or physical process within a biological entity that is part of the metabolism.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>metabolic process</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic reaction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000006 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000006">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A quality of a biochemical reaction which may proceed simultaneously in forward and backward direction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>reaction bidirectionality</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000007 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000007">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A quality of metabolic reaction to proceed in forward and backward direction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>property could be True or False</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>reaction reversibility</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000008 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000008">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000166"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000009"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chemical reaction that solely operates in a single direction, it can be forward or backward direction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>irreversible reaction</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>property or class</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>unidirectional reaction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000009 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000009">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000166"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chemical reaction that may operate simultaneously in forward and backward direction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>reversible reaction</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>bidirectional reaction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000010 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000010">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A quality of the chemical reaction that shows direction of the reaction operates, which is determined by the Gibbs free energy change.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>reaction direction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000011 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000011">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000166"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chemical reaction that proceeds from reactants to products.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>forward reaction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000012 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000012">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000166"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chemical reaction that proceeds from products to reactants.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>reverse direction</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>backward reaction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000013 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000013">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The realizable entity that is realized when the reactants and products of the chemical process are present in concentrations which have no further tendency to change with time, so that there is no observable change in the properties of the system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>At equilibrium, the reaction Gibbs energy is zero.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>chemical equilibrium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000014 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000014">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000172"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolite which is only consumed, typically the substrate(s).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>source metabolite</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000015 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000015">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000172"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolite which is only produced, typically the by-product(s).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>sink metabolite</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000016 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000016">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000198"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The flux map is typically scaled by flux magnitude and annotated with directionality.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The system biology representation that is based on quantitative visualization of reactions and metabolic fluxes within a metabolic network.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>flux map</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000017 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000017">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fluxome that indicates specific pattern or distribution of metabolic fluxes within a biological system, such as a cell or organism, under defined conditions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>flux state</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>metabolic flux phenotype</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>fluxotype</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000018 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000018">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000058"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000039"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017010"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000173"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The metabolic flux anlaysis method based on mathemetical approaches for characterizing metabolic states that constrain the possible flux space given a reaction stoichiometry.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>stoichiometry-based fluxomics method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000019 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000019">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000018"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The stoichiometry-based fluxomics method that uses set of mathematical approaches in which the possible fluxes are constrained by a minimum and maximum range of bounds, and further restrictions such as the reaction stoichiometry or objectives.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>constraint-based fluxomics method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000020 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000020">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000005"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis method that determines metabolic fluxes within a cell based on empirical data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>flux measurement method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000021 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000021">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000058"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000057"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000058"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000102"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000058"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000162"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A plan specification that quantitatively estimate/infer metabolic fluxes using a metabolic reaction model, experimental data and computation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>fluxomics method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000022 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000022">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An information content entity that contains set of all possible flux vectors that are consistent with reaction stoichiometries and a set of flux constraints at metabolic steady state.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>flux polytope</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>flux solution space</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>flux space</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>steady state flux solution space</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000023 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000023">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000159"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The data item with a list of the rates of all chemical reactions in a biological network.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>flux distribution</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>flux vector</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000024 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000024">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000226"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A representation of chemical or biological networks that uses the quantitative relationships (stoichiometry) between reactants and products.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>stoichiometric reaction model</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000025 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000025">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000236"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The reaction rate at which a specific chemical reaction proceeds from reactants to products.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>non-negative</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>forward flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000026 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000026">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000236"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The reaction rate at which a specific reaction proceeds from products to reactants.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>reverse flux</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>non-negative</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>backward flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000027 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000027">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000236"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The reaction rate that denotes the difference between the forward and backward flux for a chemical reaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>net rate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>net flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000028 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000028">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000236"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The reaction rate that denotes the minimum of the forward and backward fluxes of a chemical reaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>non-negative; This is different from exchange flux in flux balance analysis (make note in ontology)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>exchange flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000029 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000029">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The data item that represents the relative proportion of metabolic flow directed into a specific pathway at a divergence point compared to the total flow or an alternative route at that same junction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>flux ratio</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000030 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000030">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000287"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000173"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A number of degrees of freedom that represents the number of free/independent fluxes that can be varied independently within the network, which is determined by the null space of the stoichiometric matrix.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>The dimension of this null space gives the number of fluxes needed to define all other fluxes.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>degrees of freedom in stoichiometry matrix</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000031 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000031">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000170"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A molecule that has the same atomic composition (molecular formula) but different line formulae or different stereochemical formulae and hence different physical and/or chemical properties.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isomer</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000032 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000032">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data item that is the specific distribution of istopic atom in a metabolite pools at specific time.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>metabolite labeling pattern</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>isotopic labeling state</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000033 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000033">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The information content entity that describes the rate of change of an intracellular metabolite concentration is considered negligible, which holds when the metabolic flux through the metabolite pools is much larger than the change in their pool sizes over time.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Metabolic Pseudo-Steady State</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>pseudo-steady state assumption</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000034 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000034">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000177"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A steady state in which both metabolic fluxes and intracellular metabolite pool sizes are approximately constant over time.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic steady state</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000035 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000035">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A process of an isotopic labeling experiment where metabolite labeling patterns are not yet constant.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopic transient state</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000036 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000036">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000177"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A steady state when the distribution of a stable isotope label within a biological system has become and remains constant over time.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopic steady state</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000037 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000037">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000057"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fluxomics simulation that performs stochastic process for characterizing the range of possible/feasible metabolic flux vectors.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>flux state sampling</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic flux space sampling</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000038 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000038">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000035"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000162"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000059"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000021"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A completely executed planned process that studies the metabolic fluxes of the reactions in a metabolic network.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>fluxomics assay</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000039 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000039">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000162"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The fluxomics investigation that predicts physiological phenotypes allowed by the underlying metabolic model, typically enforced by a metabolic goal (e.g., maximize growth rate).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>FBA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>flux balance analysis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000040 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000040">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000162"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000038"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000046"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The fluxomics investigation that employs a quantitative strategy based on a metabolic network and experimental data to determine intracellular reaction rates (fluxes) with the highest possible accuracy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>MFA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic flux analysis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000041 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000041">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000058"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000040"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000058"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000049"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The metabolic flux analysis method that used to measure the rates of intracellular metabolic reactions in living cells using data from isotope labeling experiments.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>I-MFA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>isotope-based metabolic flux analysis method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000042 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000042">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000041"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The isotope-based metabolic flux analysis that estimates metabolic fluxes by tracking from the distribution of 13C isotopes in metabolites.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>13C-MFA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>13C-based metabolic flux analysis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>13C metabolic flux analysis method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000043 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000043">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000041"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The isotope-based metabolic flux analysis assumes isotopic steady state and metabolic steady state.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>IST-MFA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>isotopically stationary metabolic flux analysis method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000044 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000044">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000041"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The isotope-based metabolic flux analysis that assumes isotopic transient state and metabolic steady state.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>INST-13C-MFA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>INST-MFA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Isotopic Non-Stationary MFA</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>isotopically non-stationary metabolic flux analysis method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000045 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000045">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000041"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The isotope-based metabolic flux analysis that assumes both isotopic and metabolic dynamic state.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>dynamic Isotope-based metabolic flux analysis method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000046 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000046">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000178"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000049"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The experimental design and studies that aims to increase the information content of an isotope labeling experiment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotope labeling experiment design</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000047 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000047">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000046"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The isotope labeling experiment design that achieves targeted improvement of the information gain of an isotope labeling experiment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>optimal isotope labeling experimental design</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000048 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000048">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000046"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The isotope labeling experiment design that strategically choose isotopic tracers (molecule, labeling position, isotope) based on target pathway thermodynamics and atom transitions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>tracer selection</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000049 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000049">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000038"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000046"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000134"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000176"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000059"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000041"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fluxoimcs assay where biological entities are fed stable isotopic tracers (like 13C) which are then distributed throughout the metabolic network via metabolic activity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>ILE</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>SIL</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>SILE</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>Stable-isotope labeling experiment</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>fluxomics stable isotope labeling experiment</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>fluxomics isotope labeling experiment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000050 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000050">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000049"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000051"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The fluxomics isotope labeling experiment where different isotopic tracers with distinct labeling patterns or tracer mixtures are supplied to resolve overlapping metabolic routes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>parallel labeling experiments</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000051 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000051">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000049"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fluxomics isotope labeling experiment where a single tracer or tracer mixture is supplied.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>single labeling experiment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000052 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000052">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000171"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002434"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000186"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A molecular entity that is an electrically charged product of reaction of a particular parent ion.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://goldbook.iupac.org/terms/view/D01524</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>daughter ion</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>In general such ions have a direct relationship to a particular precursor ion and indeed may relate to a unique state of the precursor ion. The reaction need not necessarily involve fragmentation. It could, for example, involve a change in the number of charges carried. Thus, all fragment ions are daughter ions, but not all daughter ions are necessarily fragment ions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>product ion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000053 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000053">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000171"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002434"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000186"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A molecular entity that is an electrically charged molecular moiety which may dissociate to form fragments, one or more of which may be electrically charged, and one or more neutral species.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://goldbook.iupac.org/terms/view/P04406</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>precursor ion</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>A parent ion may be a molecular ion or an electrically charged fragment of a molecular ion.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>parent ion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000054 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000054">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000143"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopologue distribution that is of the relative abundance of different isotopomers in both a parent molecule and its fragments, obtained through tandem mass spectrometry (MS/MS).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>tandem isotopologue distribution</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000055 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000055">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017010"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000149"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>e.g. it can be represented using cumonomer representation as &quot;x1x/(x0x + x1x)&quot;.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic information that is the percentage of molecules in a given metabolite pool that contain one or more isotopic labels from a tracer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>specific enrichment</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>fractional enrichment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000056 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000056">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000148"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A zero-dimensional temporal region where a sample is taken from the biological experiment for analysis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>sampling time</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000057 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000057">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000035"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200000"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002333"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000102"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A model parameter estimation that runs a metabolic flux analysis method on a metabolic network model and/or experimental data using a fluxomics software, producing a flux solution and associated statistics.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>fluxomics simulation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000058 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000058">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000028"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A three-dimensional spatial region that is a physically or functionally distinct space (e.g., Cytosol, Mitochondria, Metabolon).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Maybe change name to biological compartment or cellular compartment</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:label>compartment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000059 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000059">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000061"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A system biology representation that defines the stoichiometric representation of cellular macromolecules (e.g. Protein, DNA, RNA, Lipids).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>biomass composition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000060 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000060">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000198"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000301"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000172"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A system biology representation that is a set of one or several metabolites.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>metabolite pool</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000061 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000061">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000198"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A system biology representation that is a metabolite pool in the metabolic network that does not have any biological counterpart and is purely introduced for modeling reason.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>pseudo metabolite pool</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000062 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000062">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An data entity that is an amount of molecular entity available to a particular metabolic process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>metabolite pool size</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000063 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000063">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000198"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000301"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000005"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A system biology representation that the aggregate of metabolic reactions in a metabolic network model.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>reaction pool</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic reaction pool</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000064 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000064">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000270"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A molecule property where certain atoms are chemically indistinguishable, making a unique atom numbering impossible.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>symmetry</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>molecular symmetry</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000065 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000065">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000198"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A system biology representation that models a metabolic reaction that does not have any biological counterpart.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>pseudo metabolic reaction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000066 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000066">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000065"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A lumped reaction is a simplified reaction that merge multiple chemical reactions into a single reaction for modeling reason.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>lumped reaction</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>lumped metabolic reaction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000067 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000067">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000065"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pseudo metabolic reaction that is an abstract reaction that represents consumption of metabolites for cellular growth in a metabolic model.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>biomass reaction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000068 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000068">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000223"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A mathematical expression that represents the limits on metabolic flux value on reactions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>linear flux constraint</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000069 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000069">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An identifier that is a unique position to atoms in a molecule to track its position within the molecule.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>atom address</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>atom identifier</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://www.inchi-trust.org/download/104/InChI_TechMan.pdf</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000070 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000070">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000226"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000154"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000301"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000166"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A representation that is the precise mapping of how each relevant atom in a substrate is rearranged to form the product metabolites during a reaction. It usually excludes hydrogens.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>atom mapping</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000071 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000071">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000155"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An object aggregate that is made of atom transitions for all reactions making up a metabolic network model.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Not a material entity. Systems biology representation</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:label>atom transition network</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000072 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000072">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The identifier that records the annotation types for atom transition.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>atom transition annotation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000073 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000073">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000072"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An atom transition annotation that uses a-z and A-Z to represent the order of the tracked atoms in a molecule.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>letter-based atom transition annotation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000074 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000074">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000072"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An atom transition annotation that uses FluxML definition to track atom mapping in a reaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>fluxml-based atom transition annotation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000075 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000075">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000072"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An atom transition annotation that uses InChI specification to track atoms in a reaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>InChI-based atom transition annotation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000076 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000076">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000072"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An atom transition annotation that uses SMILE specification to track atoms in a reaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>SMILE-based atom transition annotation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000077 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000077">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000155"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An atom transition that represents the complementary atom transition in a reaction that involves symmetric compound.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>scrambling</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>symmetric atom transition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000078 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000078">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000176"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An object aggregate that is made of differentially labeled substrate isotopomers (e.g., % [1-¹³C]glucose + % [U-¹³C]glucose) administered in an ILE.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>commercial isotopically labelled molecular entity mixture</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>tracer mixture</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>labelled source</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000079 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000079">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000176"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The quality that defines the characteristics of the isotopic tracer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopic tracer property</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000080 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000080">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000079"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>e.g. The chemical purity of 1,2-13C-Glucose is 99% meaning the glucose is 99% out of all label input.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic tracer property that is the chemical purity specified in the label input.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Could be changed to &quot;Chemical purity&quot; and moved up</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>chemical purity</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>tracer chemical purity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000081 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000081">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000079"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic tracer property that gives the price of the isotopic tracer molecular entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>All: Isotopic tracer property that defines the price of the isotopic tracer molecular entity.

BUT is this the object property? When to use it?</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Could be changed to &quot;Cost&quot; and make it general</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:label>tracer cost</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000082 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000082">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000285"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000102"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000162"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000210"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000285"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000102"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000162"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fluxomics parameter that is required to execute fluxomics software for a fluxomics investigation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>fluxomics software parameter</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000083 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000083">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000109"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A measurement datum that measures the rate of biomass formation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Te: Isn&apos;t this a quality? refer to PATO:0001492
Sergi: I don&apos;t think so, it&apos;s a number measuring how fast cells are growing. A quality does not require any process to be realized according to definition, and growth rate depends on a lot of factors and other stuff. If this was max growth rate, ir would be a realizable entity.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001492</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>growth rate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000084 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000084">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000083"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A growth rate that measures the biomass increase per unit of existing biomass per unit of time.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>specific growth rate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000085 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000085">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000109"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A measurement datum that represents the efficiency of substrate conversion into product/biomass (mass or molar basis).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>yield</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000086 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000086">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000207"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>It is used in flux estimation, specifically the variance-weighted sum of squares residuals, which is minimized to quantify fluxes. It serves as a key indicator of goodness-of-fit to reflect the certainty with which metabolic fluxes were determined.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A statistic that measures the gap between observed values and model predictions, and unlike ordinary least squares, it assigns a specific weight to each data point.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>weighted sum of squared residuals</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000087 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000087">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200000"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data transformation that used to obtain labeling data from a given metabolic models and presumed fluxes/metabolite concentrations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>forward simulation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>labeling simulation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000088 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000088">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000057"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A model parameter estimation that quantifies metabolic fluxes including their uncertainties.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>metabolic flux fitting</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic flux estimation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000089 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000089">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000216"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A statistical mdoel that is to describe how to compute a labeling measurement based on the simulated labeling state space.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>measurement model</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>It is usually represented as a matrix.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>labeling measurement model</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000090 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000090">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A measurement value of a measured quantity as obtained by a forward simulation of the metabolic network model.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>simulated measurement</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>simulated isotopic measurement</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000091 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000091">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000216"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A statistical model that is to calculate the measurement standard deviation of a simulated measurement.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>error model</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000092 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000092">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000217"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A matrix that is used to remove the contribution of naturally occurring heavy isotopes (e.g., 13C, 15N, 18O) from raw mass spectrometry data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Deconvolution matrix</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>correction matrix</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000093 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000093">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Lumped measurements are the measurements corresponding to the linear combination of two or more metabolites.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>lumped measurements</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000094 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000094">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000160"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fluxomics model parameter that is not of primary interest but must be included to correctly define the model and analyze the parameters that are of interest.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>nuisance parameter</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000095 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000095">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000094"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nuisance parameter that is to model residual naturally labeled tracer in an input pool.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>D-parameter</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000096 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000096">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000094"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nuisance parameter that is to account for residual naturally labeled fractions in a measurement group.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>G-parameter</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000097 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000097">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000223"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A mathematical expression that represents a criterion value for a proposed experimental design.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>experimental design criterion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000098 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000098">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017010"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000099"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000261"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017010"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000099"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An XML format that is defined by FluxML specification for modeling metabolic flux analysis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>FML format</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000099 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000099">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017002"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000098"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000098"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017002"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000098"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data format specification for creating, validating, and exchanging metabolic flux analysis models in 13CFlux Software.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>It is designed with the aim of providing a standard document format for creating, validating and reliable exchanging of arbitrary metabolic models across different simulation tools.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>FluxML specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000100 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000100">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000098"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017002"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000232"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data format specification that is a tabular text-based file format specification for defining metabolic reaction networks and isotopic labeling data used in 13C metabolic flux analysis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>The format is obsolete.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>FTBL specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000101 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000101">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000098"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017002"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000232"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data format specification for metabolic tracer flux data exchange in metabolic flux analysis for Influx_si software.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>MTF specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000102 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000102">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000010"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000266"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000082"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A software designed to perform, support, or facilitate metabolic flux computations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>fluxomics software</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000102"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000266"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000125"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000266"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000266"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000155"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000284"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000023"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000284"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000159"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000284"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000207"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000242"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000059"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000021"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The fluxomics software specifically designed to quantitatively estimate intracellular metabolic fluxes from an isotopic metabolic flux analysis investigation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>MFA Software</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic flux analysis software</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000104 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000104">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a MATLAB-based software for estimating TCA cycle fluxes from 13C NMR isotopomer data (Chance et al., J Biol Chem, 1983; Malloy et al., Am J Physiol, 1990).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>SIM performs forward simulation of isotopic labeling in the citric acid cycle; tcaCALC performs flux calculation by fitting simulated isotopomer patterns to observed NMR data.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>tcaCALC &amp; SIM</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://invivometabolism.org/tca.html</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000105 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000105">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a universal software framework for 13C-based metabolic flux analysis that supports modeling, simulation, design, evaluation, and statistical analysis of 13C-labeling experiments using a cumomer-based simulation approach (Wiechert et al., Metab Eng, 2001, DOI: 10.1006/mben.2001.0188).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>13CFLUX</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://www.13cflux.net/13cflux/index.html</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000106 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000106">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a third-generation, high-performance simulator supporting both isotopically stationary and non-stationary 13C-MFA, featuring dual EMU/cumomer representations, multi-isotope tracer support, Bayesian uncertainty quantification, and a Python API (Stratmann et al., Bioinformatics, 2025, DOI: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btaf630).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>13CFLUXv3</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://x3cflux.readthedocs.io/en/latest/</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000107 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000107">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that for estimating metabolic fluxes from stationary isotopic labeling data using the NLSIC algorithm, which provides more reliable convergence and better numerical accuracy than other optimization methods (Sokol et al., Bioinformatics, 2012, DOI: 10.1093/bioinformatics/bts705).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>influx_s</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://influx-si.readthedocs.io/en/latest/intro.html#influx-s</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000108 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000108">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is an extended version of influx_s that handles isotopically non-stationary labeling experiments, sharing the same NLSIC fitting algorithm and input/output formats with unconditional stability during ODE solving (Sokol et al., Bioinformatics, 2012, DOI: 10.1093/bioinformatics/bts705).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>influx_si</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://influx-si.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000109 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000109">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is an updated MATLAB-based 13C MFA software building on the INCA platform, supporting both steady-state and isotopically non-stationary MFA with the EMU framework, parallel labeling experiments, and improved computational capabilities (Young, Bioinformatics, 2014, DOI: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btu015).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>INCA2</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://mfa.vueinnovations.com/</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000110 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000110">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is an open-source MATLAB-based software for both conventional and isotopically nonstationary 13C-MFA, featuring auto-generation of metabolic models from Excel configuration worksheets and using the Levenberg-Marquardt method for flux estimation (Kajihata et al., BioMed Res Int, 2014, DOI: 10.1155/2014/627014).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>Open Mebius</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://en.metabolic-engineering.jp/page/software/openmebius</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000111 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000111">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is an open-source Python package for 13C-MFA supporting the EMU framework, INST-MFA, parallel labeling experiments, and a Bayesian Metropolis-Hastings approach, providing flexibility for custom analysis workflows and experimental design via simulation (Matsuda et al., Metab Eng Commun, 2021, DOI: 10.1016/j.mec.2021.e00177).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>mfapy</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://github.com/fumiomatsuda/mfapy</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000112 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000112">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is an extended version of OpenFLUX with support for parallel labeling experiments, extended statistical analysis, structural identifiability analysis, Monte Carlo confidence interval estimation, and experimental design optimization (Shupletsov et al., Microb Cell Fact, 2014, DOI: 10.1186/s12934-014-0152-x).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>OpenFLUX2</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://sourceforge.net/projects/openflux2/</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000113 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000113">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a Scilab-based open-source software for 13C metabolic flux analysis that provides tools for isotopomer modeling and flux estimation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>sysmetab</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://gitlab.com/scilab/forge/sysmetab/</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000114 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000114">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a MATLAB-based 13C MFA software with graphical user interface that supports steady-state 13C-MFA with user-friendly data input and flux visualization (He et al., Biotechnol Bioeng, 2016, DOI: 10.1002/bit.25958).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>WUFlux</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://tang.eece.wustl.edu/ToolDevelopment.html</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000115 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000115">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a Python-based software package for stationary 13C metabolic flux analysis to estimate intracellular flux distributions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>FluxPyt</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://sourceforge.net/projects/fluxpyt</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000116 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000116">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is an EMU-based isotope simulator that uses adjacency matrix representation to efficiently simulate isotopic labeling patterns, enabling rapid forward simulation of mass isotopomer distributions for metabolic flux analysis and experimental design (Wu et al., Front Microbiol, 2019, DOI: 10.3389/fmicb.2019.00922).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>EMUlator</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2019.00922</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000117 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000117">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a Python package for 13C metabolic flux analysis at both isotopic steady state and transient state, supporting flux estimation, labeling pattern simulation, flux balance/variability analysis, and 15N labeling data (Wu et al., ACS Synth Biol, 2023, DOI: 10.1021/acssynbio.3c00265).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>freeflux</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://github.com/Chaowu88/freeflux</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000118 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000118">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a MATLAB-based software that formulates isotope-assisted MFA as an equality-constrained nonlinear program, improving scalability and robustness compared to traditional formulations (Lugar and Sriram, PLOS Comput Biol, 2022, DOI: 10.1371/journal.pcbi.1009831).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>eiFlux</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1009831</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000119 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000119">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is a web-based server for INST-13C MFA with standardized and visual flux analysis, using evolutionary optimization in parallel and providing real-time visualization of the flux optimization process (Liu et al., Bioinformatics, 2022, DOI: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btac341).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>CeCaFlux</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://github.com/zhzhd82/CeCaFLUX</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000120 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000120">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis software that is an open-source software library for Bayesian genome-scale 13C metabolic flux analysis, using MCMC Bayesian inference with COBRApy for handling genome-scale models and supporting Two Scale 13C MFA (Backman et al., PLOS Comput Biol, 2023, DOI: 10.1371/journal.pcbi.1011111).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>BayFlux</rdfs:label>
        <foaf:homepage>https://github.com/JBEI/bayflux</foaf:homepage>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000121 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000121">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000098"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017002"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000230"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data format specification for defining metabolic models and experimental data used by the FreeFlux software package.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>Freeflux specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000122 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000122">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000098"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017002"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000231"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data format specification for defining metabolic models and experimental data used by the INCA software package.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>INCA specification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000123 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000123">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000005"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data item which represents the speed of a metabolic reaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>flux</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>it is commonly refer to flux in MFA, even though formally it is a rate. The actual definition of metabolic flux is the amount of metabolite which is converted per time unit. It is calculated as the reaction rate times stoichiometric coefficient, often normalized to a specific quantity (e.g. cell dry weight or volume of a compartment)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000124 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000124">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000004"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The metabolic flux of a metabolic reaction that occurs across metabolic network model boundaries.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>boundary flux</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>external rate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>In the FBA field, the exchange flux means the external flux.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>external flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000125 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000125">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000198"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000301"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0008150"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A system biology representation that is a model representation of metabolism, which describes the biochemical reactions occurring within a cell or organism, connecting its genome to its physiology.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic model</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000126 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000126">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A process that is the set of physical or chemical processes that occur within a living organism in order to maintain life.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>metabolism</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000127 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000127">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000125"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017002"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000278"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic model that represents a set of interconnected pathways of metabolic reactions within a biological entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>network</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>metabolic network model</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000128 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000128">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000005"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic reaction that is the transfer of a metabolite or metabolites between two compartments.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>transport reaction</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>transport process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000129 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000129">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000198"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A system biology representation that is an imaginary construct of a molecular entity that exist purely for modeling reasons (e.g. biomass).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>pseudomolecule</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000130 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000130">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000028"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A exchange flux that represents the minimum of the forward and backward fluxes of a chemical reaction, calculated by convention as a/(1+a), where a is the exchange flux.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>relative exchange flux</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000131 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000131">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000174"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>In MS, this is the output of the natural isotope abundance correction.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopologue that differs only in isotopic composition by a single element (e.g. 13C-1-glucose and 13C-2-glucose).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>tracer isotopologue</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000132 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000132">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000079"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic tracer property that denotes the labelled chemical element for the fluxomics investigation (e.g. Carbon in a 13C labelled molecular entity).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>tracer element</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000133 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000133">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data entity that describes the total number of heavy particles (protons and neutrons jointly called nucleons) in the atomic nucleus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Duplicate of monoisotopic molecular mass. Maybe make it broad synonym?</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>nucleon number</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Symbol m in mass spectrometry.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>mass number</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000134 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000134">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000171"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000079"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A molecular entity with isotopic tracer at specific atom number(s).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>isotopically labelled molecule</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>isotopically labelled molecular entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000135 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000135">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000134"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>e.g. the purchased [1-¹³C]glucose with purity of 99 atom % 13C.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopically labelled molecular entity that is the market version of the isotopically labelled molecule with manufacturer, purity and cost properties.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>commercially labelled molecule</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>commercial isotopically labelled molecular entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000136 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000136">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic information that is the input of the labelled source for the metabolic network model.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>label input</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000137 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000137">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000079"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic tracer property that specifies the atom number of the isotopic tracer in the isotopically labelled molecular entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>tracer position</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000138 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000138">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000136"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic tracer property that is the percentage of isotopically labelled molecular entity in a labelled source.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>label input proportion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000139 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000139">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000079"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>e.g. the isotopic purity for 1,2-13C-Glucose is 99% on position 1 and 2.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic tracer property that specifies the purity of the isotopic tracer in the commercial isotopically labelled molecular entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>tracer isotopic purity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000140 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000140">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic information that is the average fraction of isotopically labeled atoms in a metabolite pool, calculated as the weighted sum of isotopologue abundances divided by the maximum possible number of label incorporations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>Pierre: An average content of isotopic tracer element in the molecule that is calculated from isotopologue distribution.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>mean enrichment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017002"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000171"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An information entity that contains details necessary to describe isotope or isotopologue information.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopic information</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000142 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000142">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>e.g. percentage of 1,13C-Glucose in the total pool of Glucose in labbel input.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic information that describes the isotopic content of the molecule.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopic composition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000143 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000143">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017010"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000150"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic information that is the relative abundances of molecule isotopologues.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>ID</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>MDV</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>MID</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>isotopologue fractional abundance</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>mass ditribution vector</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>isotopologue distribution</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000144 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000144">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017010"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000148"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic information that is the abundance of isotopomers relative to the abundance of the complete set or subset of isotopic species.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopomer distribution</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000145 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000145">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000141"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0017010"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000149"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic information that is the abundance of cumomer relative to the abundance of the complete set or subset of isotopic species.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>cumomer distribution</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000146 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000146">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000226"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A representation that is of isotopic state of a metabolite.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopic state-space representation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000147 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000147">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000226"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000301"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000031"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A representation that is the space of all isotopic forms of a metabolite.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopic state-space</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000148 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000148">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000146"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic state-space representation that models positional labeling by a binary number (0: non-labeled, 1: labeled).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>isotopomer representation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000149 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000149">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000146"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic state-space representation that models positional labeling by a state based on three possibilities: 0 represents unlabeled, 1 represents labeled or x: either labeled or unlabeled.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>cumomer representation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000150 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000150">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000146"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An isotopic state-space representation that models the mass differences due to labeling of a compound fragment. The fragment is defined by a binary number (position is/is not part of the fragment).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>EMU</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>elementary metabolite unit representation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000151 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000151">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000109"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A measurement datum that measures the number of a particular countable entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000070</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>amount</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000152 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000152">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000068"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A linear flux constraint that is the fixed value for linear combination of fluxes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>flux equality constraint</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000153 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000153">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000068"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A linear flux constraint that represents the upper or lower bound of linear combinations of fluxes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>flux inequality constraint</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000154 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000154">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000226"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000301"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000171"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A representation that consists of a set of all atom identifiers considered for a molecule.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>atom map</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000155 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000155">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000226"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000070"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The representation that records the precise bijection of how each relevant atom identifier in a substrate is rearranged to form the product during a reaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>atom transition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000156 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000156">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000207"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A statistic that is the inherent variability of repeated observation measurements of a quantity including quantities evaluated by statistical methods and by other means.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C71478</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>measurement uncertainty</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000157 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000157">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000005"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A metabolic flux analysis method that is used to quantify the flux uncertainty estimate.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>flux uncertainty quantification method</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000158 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000158">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000207"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A statistic that quantify the uncertainty of the flux solution.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>flux uncertainty estimate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000159 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000159">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000027"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000058"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000016"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A data entity that specifies the parameters including flux vector and other parameters (e.g. metabolite pool sizes and model parameters) that best explains experimental data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>flux solution</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000160 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000160">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000210"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fluxomics parameter that are necessary to run fluxomics labeling simulation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>model parameter</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>fluxomics model parameter</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000161 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000161">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FLUXO_0000094"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nuisance parameter that is to scale measurements of a measurement group to better fit simulated measurements.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>groupscale</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


